### 2.2 Data Standardization & Feature Engineering

Features were extracted from the {{ nsites_word }} OMOP CDM v5.4 databases.{% if features.n_columns %} The feature table has {{ features.n_columns }} columns; after removing identifiers, the outcome{% if features.empty %} and {{ features.empty | length | words }} columns with no observed values ({{ features.empty | join(', ') }}){% endif %}, {{ features.n }} features entered the models{% if features.n_binary is not none and features.n_continuous is not none %} ({{ features.n_binary }} binary, {{ features.n_continuous }} continuous){% endif %}:{% else %} {{ features.n }} features entered the models:{% endif %}

- Demographic Features: Age (categories 18–44, 45–64, 65–74, 75+), sex, race, ethnicity, Social Deprivation Index (SDI quintiles 1–5), RUCA urban/rural codes, and BMI classifications. Each site's address history is loaded into the OMOP location table, and each stay is assigned the address in effect at admission (otherwise the latest earlier address, otherwise the earliest). The address ZIP code is linked to the RUCA primary code (original coding: 1 metropolitan, 2 micropolitan, 3 and above small town or rural) and to the 2015–2019 ZIP-level Social Deprivation Index score, which is cut into quintiles over the cohort. Stays without a usable ZIP code are reported as Missing/Unknown rather than assigned a reference category.
- Discharge Status: Home, home health, skilled nursing or rehabilitation facility, against medical advice, other (for example hospice or assisted living), or missing / unknown when the source record carries no discharge status (PCORnet NI, UN or blank), read from the index stay's OMOP discharge concept and, where that is unmapped, its source value.
- Vital Signs: Mean systolic and diastolic blood pressure and BMI recorded between admission and discharge of the index stay.
- Laboratory Measures (Index Stay Mean): The mean of the laboratory measurements recorded between admission and discharge of the index stay, matched across health systems through the OMOP vocabulary hierarchy (each laboratory is a concept set built from concept_ancestor, not a hand-picked list of LOINC codes) and restricted to physiologically plausible ranges. Panels include {{ lr.labs | join_and }}.
- Medication Exposure (OMOP Drug Exposure): Exposure in the 365 days before discharge to 8 therapeutic classes, assigned by rolling branded and clinical drugs up to their ingredients: Biguanides (Metformin), Insulins, Sulfonylureas, RAAS Inhibitors (ACE inhibitors / ARBs), Antihypertensives, Beta Blockers, Systemic Corticosteroids, and Lipid Modifying Agents (Statins).
- Comorbidity Indices: 31 Elixhauser comorbidity domains from ICD-9-CM and ICD-10-CM diagnosis codes recorded on or before the index discharge date (all available history, including diagnoses coded during the index stay), and the number of distinct conditions recorded before the index admission.
- Historical Healthcare Utilization: Counts of visits in the 365 days before admission (prior_IP_OS_ED_count for inpatient, observation and emergency visits combined, prior inpatient stays, prior emergency visits, all prior encounters), summed prior inpatient length of stay, days since the prior encounter (set to 365 when there was none), and readmission_count_twelve_months, which counts inpatient stays in the prior 365 days. The number of distinct condition concepts recorded during the index stay (n_secondary_dx_ccs) and the index length of stay complete the utilization features.

