### 2.3 Preprocessing, Imputation & Feature Scaling

To maintain strict separation of training and evaluation data and prevent out-of-fold information overlap, preprocessing steps were executed within each cross-validation fold:

1. Imputation & Multicollinearity Defenses: Missing values in the model matrix (laboratory, vital sign and other continuous features) were imputed using median values calculated strictly on training folds and applied to test folds. Tree-based ensembles (XGBoost, HistGBM, Random Forest) natively handle correlated feature pairs (e.g., BUN and creatinine, hemoglobin and hematocrit); for the Logistic Regression benchmark model, L2-ridge regularization ({{ hyper['Logistic Regression'].text or 'C=1.0' }}) was applied to stabilize coefficient estimation.
2. Scaling & Odds Ratio Interpretation: In the benchmark, continuous features were Z-score standardized (fit on training folds) for Logistic Regression only; the tree-based models use unscaled features. The multivariable Logistic Regression table was fit separately by unpenalized maximum likelihood on the whole cohort, and its coefficients were back-transformed to the original units. Standardized Beta coefficients (β~std~ = β~raw~ × SD~X~, the change in log-odds per one standard deviation) are reported to rank relative feature importance across disparate clinical scales, while Adjusted Odds Ratios (OR = exp(β~raw~ × Δ)) are reported {% if decisions.table6_increments == "sd" %}per one standard deviation of each continuous feature{% else %}per a clinically meaningful increment Δ (e.g., 10 mmHg of blood pressure, 10 mg/dL of BUN, 5 mEq/L of sodium, 10 outpatient encounters){% endif %} or, for indicator variables, for presence versus absence.{% if decisions.table6_missing == "indicator" %} In that table, a laboratory value or vital sign missing for at least 11 stays enters with a "not measured" indicator next to it: its missing values are set to the mean of the measured stays, so its odds ratio is estimated from the stays where it was measured, and the indicator carries the difference of the unmeasured stays. A laboratory is measured because a clinician ordered it, so whether it was measured carries risk information of its own. Indicators that coincide (eGFR is computed from creatinine, so both are missing in the same stays) enter as one term.{% elif decisions.table6_missing == "median" %} In that table, missing continuous values were median-imputed.{% endif %}


