### 3.{{ ns.res }} Multivariable Risk Factors & Odds Ratio Benchmark

Multivariable Logistic Regression odds ratios and 95% confidence intervals across all {{ lr.n_terms }} model terms (including discharge disposition and index laboratory values) are presented in {{ ref.lr }}. The model was fit by unpenalized maximum likelihood on the {{ cohort.n | n }} patients' randomly drawn stays, so observations are independent; the 95% confidence intervals are Wald intervals from the model-based standard errors. To facilitate clinical interpretation and cross-variable comparison, Adjusted Odds Ratios ({% if decisions.table6_increments == "sd" %}per one standard deviation for continuous features{% else %}per the clinical increment shown in the Increment column{% endif %}) and Standardized Beta coefficients (per 1 SD) are presented side-by-side, to two decimal places, with features grouped in the order of {{ ref.table1 }} (comorbidities and other clinical features follow the laboratory values). Each multilevel feature (age, race, SDI, RUCA, discharge status, tobacco use and BMI) is shown with its reference category (OR 1.00), against which its other levels are compared. This table is an association model fit on the whole cohort at its natural prevalence, not one of the balanced-training prediction models.

